## Skill

Use `$plan-em`.

It turns an approved PRD into an engineering plan and selects the specialist engineering agents needed. It defaults to team mode, where an orchestrator divides the work among specialists.

## The approval it asks for

Before activating any specialists, it shows:

- A short summary of the PRD’s product intent.
- A roster table covering each proposed agent, domain, scope, and PRD features.
- One choice: **Approve roster** or **Revise roster**.

This roster approval is the normal run’s single human gate. It does not ask you to choose the execution mode or project size; those have defaults or are derived automatically.

Extra questions appear only in exceptional cases, such as an unfinished prior run, a genuine dependency conflict, an unsupported platform, or a product decision that automated certification cannot resolve.

